# Documents, in Zathura. The org.pwmt.zathura-pdf-mupdf entry is the one that
# declares these types; org.pwmt.zathura.desktop declares none at all. Zathura's
# entry also claims image/png, image/jpeg, image/bmp, image/tiff and
# image/svg+xml — those stay with Loupe above, since Zathura's image support
# exists to render pages, not to be where a photo opens.
application/pdf=org.pwmt.zathura-pdf-mupdf.desktop
application/oxps=org.pwmt.zathura-pdf-mupdf.desktop
application/epub+zip=org.pwmt.zathura-pdf-mupdf.desktop
application/x-fictionbook=org.pwmt.zathura-pdf-mupdf.desktop
application/x-mobipocket-ebook=org.pwmt.zathura-pdf-mupdf.desktop

# Office documents, in OnlyOffice. The list is the MimeType= line of
# onlyoffice-desktopeditors.desktop, less the types this file already answers
# for, so the list cannot claim a format OnlyOffice will not open.
#
# There is one block rather than one per component. OnlyOffice ships a single
# desktop entry for the whole suite and picks the editor from the opened file's
# type inside one process, so there is no per-component entry to name — where
# LibreOffice needed five, this needs one, and the document still arrives in the
# right kind of editor.
#
# Seven types the entry declares are left where they already were:
# application/pdf, application/oxps and application/epub+zip stay in Zathura,
# and text/plain, text/csv, text/markdown and text/tab-separated-values stay in
# Neovide. text/csv-schema is Neovide's alone — OnlyOffice does not declare it.
#
# FictionBook stays in Zathura too, and is the one exclusion that is not a
# straight overlap. Zathura holds application/x-fictionbook; OnlyOffice declares
# application/x-fictionbook+xml, which /usr/share/mime/aliases gives as the
# canonical name of that same type. It is one format, so it keeps one handler,
# and an e-book belongs with the document viewer.
#
# application/vnd.ms-xpsdocument is here while application/oxps stays with
# Zathura, which reads like an oversight and is not: XPS and OpenXPS are
# different types, and each entry declares only its own. image/vnd.djvu is here
# for the same reason — this build of Zathura declares no DjVu type at all.
#
# What LibreOffice answered for and nothing now does: the legacy word processor
# and spreadsheet formats it carried import filters for — WordPerfect, AbiWord,
# Lotus 1-2-3, StarOffice, dBASE, Gnumeric, Parquet, the iWork sidecar types and
# the ODF master documents — the formula formats Math opened, and every drawing
# format but .odg and the Visio family. Those 81 types are not mapped here.
# Pointing them at OnlyOffice would trade a double-click that does nothing for
# an error dialog from a program that never claimed the format; both fail, and
# only one of them fails honestly.
application/msword=onlyoffice-desktopeditors.desktop
application/msword-template=onlyoffice-desktopeditors.desktop
application/rtf=onlyoffice-desktopeditors.desktop
application/vnd.apple.keynote=onlyoffice-desktopeditors.desktop
application/vnd.apple.numbers=onlyoffice-desktopeditors.desktop
application/vnd.apple.pages=onlyoffice-desktopeditors.desktop
application/vnd.ms-excel=onlyoffice-desktopeditors.desktop
application/vnd.ms-excel.sheet.binary.macroEnabled.12=onlyoffice-desktopeditors.desktop
application/vnd.ms-excel.sheet.macroEnabled.12=onlyoffice-desktopeditors.desktop
application/vnd.ms-excel.template.macroEnabled.12=onlyoffice-desktopeditors.desktop
application/vnd.ms-powerpoint=onlyoffice-desktopeditors.desktop
application/vnd.ms-powerpoint.presentation.macroEnabled.12=onlyoffice-desktopeditors.desktop
application/vnd.ms-powerpoint.slideshow.macroEnabled.12=onlyoffice-desktopeditors.desktop
application/vnd.ms-powerpoint.template.macroEnabled.12=onlyoffice-desktopeditors.desktop
application/vnd.ms-visio.drawing.macroEnabled.main+xml=onlyoffice-desktopeditors.desktop
